  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The emergency terms go to competitors",
      "severity": "Critical",
      "finding": "You rank 14th for \"emergency plumber toronto\" (1,900 searches a month) and do not appear in the first five pages for \"burst pipe repair toronto\" (590 a month). Both are terms firstrankplumbing.ca holds in the top three.",
      "why": "You told us emergency callouts are your most profitable work and that most inquiries arrive by phone. These are the searches made by someone who will call the first number they find, and they are not finding yours.",
      "teaser": "Closing this is a service-page and local-signal problem rather than a content-volume one — it is the first thing the SEO engagement would address, because it is the shortest path to calls."
    },
    {
      "title": "Twenty-three pages have no meta description",
      "severity": "High",
      "finding": "23 of 41 indexed pages have no meta description, including the service pages for drain cleaning and water-heater installation.",
      "why": "Google writes its own snippet when there is nothing to use, and the sentence it picks is the one that decides whether somebody clicks you or the result above you.",
      "teaser": "A pass over the indexed pages is part of the technical SEO work and does not depend on anything else being fixed first."
    }
  ],
